AAOS 2024 identifies MRI as the preferred modality for suspected acute meniscal tears (Strong recommendation; High evidence quality).

Orthopedic metadata v1:
{"application_conditions":["Clinician review of the stated source population and context is required."],"body_region":"knee","limitations":["No automatic imaging order or interpretation; this scope does not include all chronic knee pain."],"orthopedic_schema_version":"1.0.0","source_keys":["aaos_meniscus_2024"],"topic":"meniscus"}

AAOS 2024 consensus highlights displaced acute tears restricting movement as potential candidates for acute specialist surgical assessment.

Orthopedic metadata v1:
{"application_conditions":["Clinician review of the stated source population and context is required."],"body_region":"knee","limitations":["Consensus option with Very Low evidence quality; reported locking alone does not confirm a displaced tear."],"orthopedic_schema_version":"1.0.0","source_keys":["aaos_meniscus_2024"],"topic":"meniscus"}

ESCAPE found exercise-based physical therapy noninferior to partial meniscectomy for five-year knee function in its enrolled degenerative-tear population.

