AAOS 2023 supports considering MRI to characterize a known knee OCD lesion on radiographs or suspected concomitant pathology (High recommendation strength).

Orthopedic metadata v1:
{"application_conditions":["Clinician review of the stated source population and context is required."],"body_region":"knee","limitations":["Specific to knee OCD, not every knee pain presentation or cartilage abnormality."],"orthopedic_schema_version":"1.0.0","source_keys":["aaos_ocd_2023"],"topic":"cartilage_osteochondral"}

For symptomatic unstable/displaced knee OCD, AAOS 2023 offers surgery as an option in immature and mature patients (Limited strength).

Orthopedic metadata v1:
{"application_conditions":["Clinician review of the stated source population and context is required."],"body_region":"knee","limitations":["Symptoms, maturity and stability require specialist review; no procedure is chosen automatically."],"orthopedic_schema_version":"1.0.0","source_keys":["aaos_ocd_2023"],"topic":"cartilage_osteochondral"}

